1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,510
A two mark favourite.

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:08,945
Galvanising protects even when scratched, because zinc is more reactive than iron and corrodes first.

3
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:16,380
A scratched tin can rusts faster than bare iron, because now iron is the more reactive metal and becomes the anode.

